-- run: `backend.md` §9 item 1's zero-use rule, which is the half that is
-- about correctness rather than bytes — and the one fixture in the corpus
-- whose dev and release output legitimately DIFFER.
--
-- §9 item 1: "a binding whose value is never used may be dropped whole,
-- everything inside it included, a `Debug.log` among it". `language.md` §6's
-- *What an optimiser may assume* is the licence in so many words, and
-- `Debug.log` is the one thing in the language that can see it being spent.
--
-- Three `Debug.log`s in `report`, in written order:
--
--   1. `first` is read, so it survives and prints;
--   2. `ignored` is read by NOTHING. A release build drops the binding whole
--      and the line does not appear. A dev build keeps it — elimination is
--      declaration-granular and does not look inside a body (§9's
--      reachability walk), so `local dead bindings` is release-only and dev
--      still prints it;
--   3. `second` is read, so it survives and prints AFTER the first: the
--      surviving order did not move, which is the other half of the claim.
--
-- Hence `ReleaseDeadDebug.expected` and `ReleaseDeadDebug.release-expected`.
-- That pair is the whole of the difference between the two builds across the
-- corpus, and it is deliberate rather than tolerated: §9 asks for the drop by
-- name, and a `.release-expected` is how a fixture says so out loud instead
-- of a harness quietly accepting two answers everywhere.
--
-- `dropped` is the third kind and belongs to `run/DceDebugLog`: a whole
-- declaration nothing reaches, deleted by the reachability walk in BOTH
-- builds, so neither golden has its line.
import Node exposing (Program)
import String


log : String, Int -> Int
log label v =
    Debug.log v label


pub dropped : Int
dropped =
    log "dead.declaration" 99


report : Int -> Int
report n =
    let
        first =
            log "dead.first" n

        ignored =
            log "dead.ignored" (n * 10)

        second =
            log "dead.second" (n + 1)
    in
    first + second


main : Program
main =
    Node.printLines [ String.fromInt (report 2) ]
